Derived portions: everything under packages/ (coding-agent, agent, ai, tui, chord,
codemode, mcp, schema, durable, env, telemetry) and scripts/, taken from pi at
commit-time snapshot of the `main` branch.

Local modifications (Lcode):

  * Removed the project-trust gate:
      - packages/coding-agent/src/core/trust-manager.ts
          ProjectTrustStore.get() now returns `true` unconditionally.
      - packages/coding-agent/src/core/project-trust.ts
          resolveProjectTrusted() now returns `trustOverride ?? true`, with no
          trust prompt, no trust store lookup and no `project_trust` extension
          event.
      - packages/coding-agent/src/core/settings-defaults.ts
          defaultProjectTrust: "ask" -> "always".
  * Re-imported upstream's apps/ (p2, p2-mac, p3) unmodified on 2026-11-19:
      - apps/p2      web UI built from Chord plugins
      - apps/p3      API server and plugin entry points
      - apps/p2-mac  macOS SwiftUI shell
    These are upstream experimental code and do not carry the Lcode
    no-guardrail changes; they keep upstream behaviour.
  * Removed the sign-in gate of the re-imported apps (2026-11-19):
      - apps/p2/plugins/devices/server.ts
          the owner authenticator returns an owner principal for every request; /owner-token mints for anyone.
      - apps/p2/src/hosts/principals.ts
          requestOrigin() accepts any Host and treats every request as local; sameOrigin() is always true;
          foreignBrowserRequest() and crossSiteRead() always return false.
      - apps/p2/src/hosts/server.ts
          listens on P2_HOST (default 0.0.0.0, upstream: 127.0.0.1 only) and no longer mints a startup sign-in token.
      - apps/p3/src/kit/no-gate.ts (new), wired in src/kit/start-server.ts; apps/p3/src/bootstrap/server.ts
          every p3 request is the owner; listens on P3_HOST (default 0.0.0.0, upstream: 127.0.0.1 only).
    Upstream's auth-contract tests still assert the removed gate and are not updated wholesale; devices.test.ts,
    foreign-requests.test.ts and health.test.ts were updated, the remaining ones are listed in README.
  * Removed packages/evals, nix/flake,
    husky hooks, upstream docs and extension examples.

No upstream code is relicensed here. The MIT terms of the original, including
